      "body": "Although these mHC tests pass on the B200 CI machine, they fail on SM120 for two numerical reasons:\r\n\r\n1. TF32-sensitive references. PyTorch FP32 matrix multiplications may use TF32 when matmul precision is  \"high\" , making the reference insufficiently precise for comparisons against FP32 kernels. The tests now explicitly use  \"highest\"  and restore the previous setting afterward.\r\n2. BF16 rounding differences. Small post-stage rounding differences can cause the final comparison to fail. The unfused path now checks post separately and compares pre using the same BF16 residual.\r\n\r\nThese are test-reference fixes; production kernels and tolerances remain unchanged. The mechanisms were reproduced locally on SM120; ",
